 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 1.6445144097222189,
   "end": 3.499014409722219,
   "text": "Look up at the night sky."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.799014409722219,
   "end": 7.102347743055552,
   "text": "Near the southern horizon, a bright star shines."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.402347743055553,
   "end": 10.367681076388886,
   "text": "It looks calm. It looks close. It is not."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.667681076388885,
   "end": 15.766347743055551,
   "text": "That point of light is Alpha Centauri, the nearest star system to our Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 16.06634774305555,
   "end": 20.952502572601006,
   "text": "And the journey to reach it may be the most terrifying voyage humanity has"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.952502572601006,
   "end": 21.87691024305555,
   "text": "ever imagined."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.176910243055552,
   "end": 24.926056076388885,
   "text": "In the next eight minutes, we will fly there."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.226056076388886,
   "end": 30.519096354166663,
   "text": "We will cross 40 trillion kilometres of darkness, and meet the dangers waiting"
  },
  {
   "start": 30.519096354166663,
   "end": 31.333410243055553,
   "text": "in the void."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.633410243055554,
   "end": 36.38284774305556,
   "text": "Stay until the end, because the last part changes how you see the stars."
  },
  {
   "start": 39.710031770833325,
   "end": 44.209073437499995,
   "text": "Let's start with the farthest explorer we have ever sent toward the stars."
  },
  {
   "start": 44.50907343749999,
   "end": 52.611760937499994,
   "text": "Voyager 1 launched in 1977, and entered interstellar space in 2012."
  },
  {
   "start": 52.91176093749999,
   "end": 58.42348580163043,
   "text": "It travels at about seventeen kilometres every second, many times faster than"
  },
  {
   "start": 58.42348580163043,
   "end": 59.49719843749999,
   "text": "a rifle bullet."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.79719843749999,
   "end": 64.62809448341837,
   "text": "Yet if it were aimed at Alpha Centauri, it would need around seventy-five"
  },
  {
   "start": 64.62809448341837,
   "end": 66.28251093749999,
   "text": "thousand years to arrive."
  },
  {
   "start": 66.58251093749999,
   "end": 72.63184427083333,
   "text": "Seventy-five thousand years ago, no city, no farm, and no written word existed"
  },
  {
   "start": 72.63184427083333,
   "end": 74.02784427083333,
   "text": "anywhere on Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 74.32784427083332,
   "end": 79.58877356376262,
   "text": "Even the Parker Solar Probe, the fastest machine ever built, would take nearly"
  },
  {
   "start": 79.58877356376262,
   "end": 81.00517760416666,
   "text": "seven thousand years."
  },
  {
   "start": 84.33236163194442,
   "end": 86.27369496527776,
   "text": "So how far is it, really?"
  },
  {
   "start": 86.57369496527775,
   "end": 91.28513246527775,
   "text": "Alpha Centauri lies about 4.37 light years away."
  },
  {
   "start": 91.58513246527775,
   "end": 96.89713246527775,
   "text": "Light, the fastest thing in the universe, needs more than four years to make this trip."
  },
  {
   "start": 97.19713246527775,
   "end": 100.54011163194441,
   "text": "In kilometres, that is roughly forty trillion."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.84011163194441,
   "end": 105.82601639384917,
   "text": "Or, in units our Solar System understands, about two hundred and seventy"
  },
  {
   "start": 105.82601639384917,
   "end": 109.56544496527775,
   "text": "thousand times the distance from the Earth to the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 109.86544496527775,
   "end": 114.72288086271364,
   "text": "Shrink the Sun to a single grain of sand, and the next star would still be"
  },
  {
   "start": 114.72288086271364,
   "end": 116.69211163194441,
   "text": "nearly thirty kilometres away."
  },
  {
   "start": 120.01929565972218,
   "end": 122.96031649305552,
   "text": "And what waits there? Not one star, but three."
  },
  {
   "start": 123.26031649305551,
   "end": 129.0506574021464,
   "text": "Alpha Centauri A and B are sun-like stars that circle each other once every"
  },
  {
   "start": 129.0506574021464,
   "end": 133.4513164930555,
   "text": "eighty years, roughly as far apart as the Sun and Uranus."
  },
  {
   "start": 133.7513164930555,
   "end": 139.23198939025175,
   "text": "Far beyond them, about a fifth of a light year away, a small red dwarf called"
  },
  {
   "start": 139.23198939025175,
   "end": 141.36731649305548,
   "text": "Proxima Centauri drifts along."
  },
  {
   "start": 141.6673164930555,
   "end": 146.90729565972217,
   "text": "At 4.24 light years, Proxima is the closest star to us of all."
  },
  {
   "start": 147.20729565972215,
   "end": 151.42167065972214,
   "text": "Yet it is so dim that you can never see it without a telescope."
  },
  {
   "start": 154.74885468749991,
   "end": 159.86193802083324,
   "text": "Around that little star circles a world astronomers cannot stop thinking about."
  },
  {
   "start": 160.16193802083325,
   "end": 165.91365418513584,
   "text": "Proxima b, discovered in 2016, is a rocky planet with roughly the mass of"
  },
  {
   "start": 165.91365418513584,
   "end": 171.2714171874999,
   "text": "Earth, sitting in the habitable zone where liquid water could exist."
  },
  {
   "start": 171.57141718749992,
   "end": 176.68658699882067,
   "text": "But look closer. It orbits its star every eleven days, about eight times"
  },
  {
   "start": 176.68658699882067,
   "end": 179.10208385416658,
   "text": "closer than Mercury is to our Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 179.4020838541666,
   "end": 185.99358773013557,
   "text": "And its star is violent. In March 2017, a single flare made Proxima a thousand"
  },
  {
   "start": 185.99358773013557,
   "end": 190.30341718749992,
   "text": "times brighter in radio light, in just ten seconds."
  },
  {
   "start": 190.60341718749993,
   "end": 195.3550838541666,
   "text": "Flares like that could strip away an atmosphere, and sterilise a surface."
  },
  {
   "start": 195.6550838541666,
   "end": 201.90200001270318,
   "text": "And around Alpha Centauri A, the James Webb telescope spotted a faint dot in"
  },
  {
   "start": 201.90200001270318,
   "end": 208.06671990599585,
   "text": "2024: a possible giant planet, about twice as far from its star as Earth is"
  },
  {
   "start": 208.06671990599585,
   "end": 209.13527135416658,
   "text": "from the Sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.43527135416662,
   "end": 215.25477135416662,
   "text": "It was seen only once. For now, it remains a candidate, not a confirmed world."
  },
  {
   "start": 218.58195538194434,
   "end": 222.11391371527768,
   "text": "So the destination is real. The problem is speed."
  },
  {
   "start": 222.4139137152777,
   "end": 227.04701175449338,
   "text": "To arrive within a human lifetime, we would need to travel at a serious"
  },
  {
   "start": 227.04701175449338,
   "end": 229.0699137152777,
   "text": "fraction of the speed of light."
  },
  {
   "start": 229.36991371527768,
   "end": 234.29974228670625,
   "text": "At ten percent of light speed, the trip takes about forty-four years. At"
  },
  {
   "start": 234.29974228670625,
   "end": 236.559247048611,
   "text": "twenty percent, about twenty-two."
  },
  {
   "start": 236.859247048611,
   "end": 241.54201788194433,
   "text": "But rockets that carry their own fuel cannot come close to those speeds."
  },
  {
   "start": 241.84201788194434,
   "end": 247.4313512152777,
   "text": "So engineers asked a radical question: what if the ship carried no fuel at all?"
  },
  {
   "start": 250.7585352430554,
   "end": 256.3186746400744,
   "text": "In 2016, Yuri Milner announced, alongside Stephen Hawking, Breakthrough"
  },
  {
   "start": 256.3186746400744,
   "end": 260.3908894097221,
   "text": "Starshot, a hundred million dollar research program."
  },
  {
   "start": 260.6908894097221,
   "end": 266.40822274305543,
   "text": "The idea: build the most powerful laser array ever made, around a hundred gigawatts."
  },
  {
   "start": 266.70822274305544,
   "end": 271.76128696323894,
   "text": "Then use it to push a fleet of tiny probes, each a chip weighing about a gram,"
  },
  {
   "start": 271.76128696323894,
   "end": 273.76955607638877,
   "text": "attached to a mirror-like sail."
  },
  {
   "start": 274.0695560763888,
   "end": 278.8177020617902,
   "text": "In just minutes, the laser would blast them up to twenty percent of the speed"
  },
  {
   "start": 278.8177020617902,
   "end": 282.51755607638876,
   "text": "of light, more than two hundred million kilometres per hour."
  },
  {
   "start": 282.81755607638877,
   "end": 286.5192644097221,
   "text": "They would reach Alpha Centauri in about twenty years."
  },
  {
   "start": 286.8192644097221,
   "end": 290.9771810763888,
   "text": "And their pictures would need another four years to travel home."
  },
  {
   "start": 294.30436510416655,
   "end": 297.4608859374999,
   "text": "But the space between the stars is not empty."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.7608859374999,
   "end": 301.5441984374999,
   "text": "It is filled with thin gas, and tiny grains of dust."
  },
  {
   "start": 301.84419843749987,
   "end": 307.01936342066483,
   "text": "At normal speeds, they are harmless. At twenty percent of light speed, every"
  },
  {
   "start": 307.01936342066483,
   "end": 308.5855317708332,
   "text": "grain becomes a bullet."
  },
  {
   "start": 308.8855317708332,
   "end": 314.1317609374999,
   "text": "A single sail could be struck by around a billion dust particles on the way."
  },
  {
   "start": 314.43176093749986,
   "end": 320.5084807956559,
   "text": "And a grain just one millimetre across would hit with the energy of dozens of"
  },
  {
   "start": 320.5084807956559,
   "end": 321.8500942708332,
   "text": "kilograms of TNT."
  },
  {
   "start": 322.15009427083316,
   "end": 327.53288214962106,
   "text": "A big ship could be destroyed in an instant. For the tiny sails, the plan is a"
  },
  {
   "start": 327.53288214962106,
   "end": 331.2594276041665,
   "text": "numbers game: launch thousands, and hope some survive."
  },
  {
   "start": 334.5866116319443,
   "end": 337.52871579861096,
   "text": "There is a second killer, and you cannot see it."
  },
  {
   "start": 337.828715798611,
   "end": 343.5699139968092,
   "text": "Space is threaded with cosmic rays, fast charged particles that raise the risk"
  },
  {
   "start": 343.5699139968092,
   "end": 345.99888246527763,
   "text": "of cancer even on short missions."
  },
  {
   "start": 346.29888246527764,
   "end": 351.8356360572317,
   "text": "At relativistic speed, it gets worse: even a single hydrogen atom slams in so"
  },
  {
   "start": 351.8356360572317,
   "end": 356.7252366319443,
   "text": "hard that, from the ship's point of view, it acts like a cosmic ray."
  },
  {
   "start": 357.0252366319443,
   "end": 362.21766120090984,
   "text": "Analyses of fast starships find that a crew at very high speed would need a"
  },
  {
   "start": 362.21766120090984,
   "end": 367.0639241319443,
   "text": "shield several metres thick, just to survive the gas it flies through."
  },
  {
   "start": 370.39110815972214,
   "end": 375.9478237560524,
   "text": "Now imagine the impossible: a crewed ship that accelerates at one g, the same"
  },
  {
   "start": 375.9478237560524,
   "end": 378.2571081597221,
   "text": "pull you feel standing on Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 378.55710815972213,
   "end": 381.3848998263888,
   "text": "Halfway there, it flips around, and brakes."
  },
  {
   "start": 381.6848998263888,
   "end": 385.95156649305545,
   "text": "No engine we know could do this. But the physics is clear."
  },
  {
   "start": 386.25156649305546,
   "end": 391.62756649305544,
   "text": "The crew would age about three and a half years, while about six years pass on Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 391.92756649305545,
   "end": 396.8768998263888,
   "text": "At the midpoint, they would be moving at ninety-five percent of the speed of light."
  },
  {
   "start": 397.17689982638876,
   "end": 402.64781508062606,
   "text": "Outside the window, the stars crowd into a blazing blue ring ahead, while the"
  },
  {
   "start": 402.64781508062606,
   "end": 405.5608998263888,
   "text": "sky behind fades to a dull, red darkness."
  },
  {
   "start": 408.88808385416655,
   "end": 413.02258385416656,
   "text": "If a Starshot probe survives, it gets exactly one chance."
  },
  {
   "start": 413.32258385416657,
   "end": 418.3669164434523,
   "text": "It cannot slow down. It will tear through the system at about thirty-five"
  },
  {
   "start": 418.3669164434523,
   "end": 421.0618338541666,
   "text": "times the Earth–Sun distance every day."
  },
  {
   "start": 421.36183385416655,
   "end": 426.3956954893867,
   "text": "In those few precious hours, its tiny camera would take the first close-up"
  },
  {
   "start": 426.3956954893867,
   "end": 428.5725005208332,
   "text": "pictures of another star system."
  },
  {
   "start": 428.8725005208332,
   "end": 433.76697671130944,
   "text": "Then a one-watt laser would send them home, a whisper crossing four light"
  },
  {
   "start": 433.76697671130944,
   "end": 434.97383385416657,
   "text": "years of darkness."
  },
  {
   "start": 435.2738338541666,
   "end": 439.0498338541666,
   "text": "And after that, the probe vanishes into the dark, forever."
  },
  {
   "start": 442.3770178819444,
   "end": 445.66235121527774,
   "text": "So, is the journey to Alpha Centauri possible?"
  },
  {
   "start": 445.96235121527775,
   "end": 450.9733095486111,
   "text": "Not yet. Dust, radiation, and the sheer distance still stand in the way."
  },
  {
   "start": 451.2733095486111,
   "end": 455.93746049200735,
   "text": "But the first steps are happening right now: the lasers, the sails, and the"
  },
  {
   "start": 455.93746049200735,
   "end": 457.8653095486111,
   "text": "telescopes hunting for planets."
  },
  {
   "start": 458.1653095486111,
   "end": 462.22191371527776,
   "text": "We are a species that once crossed oceans in wooden boats."
  },
  {
   "start": 462.5219137152778,
   "end": 466.95035121527775,
   "text": "The ocean between the stars is wider, and darker, and colder."
  },
  {
   "start": 467.25035121527776,
   "end": 470.61466371527774,
   "text": "But the nearest shore is only four light years away."
  },
  {
   "start": 470.91466371527775,
   "end": 475.807951850871,
   "text": "If you enjoyed this journey, subscribe to Technical Talk India, and tell us in"
  },
  {
   "start": 475.807951850871,
   "end": 478.31733038194443,
   "text": "the comments: would you board that ship?"
  }
 ]
}